{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery","id":815175,"title":"On Chambers: A Few Questions About Load-Bearing Scenery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T18:53:07-08:00","id":815175,"title":"On Chambers: A Few Questions About Load-Bearing Scenery","content":"Just a few questions on how a Lair's Chambers function.<br /> <br /> 1. Rules are given for antagonists collapsing a Lair's Chambers, but how would they know such a thing was possible in the first place (excepting Heroes, who would probably intuit it the same way they do Anathemas)?<br /> <br /> 2. How large are Chambers? Do they have a set size limit, or is it more of a &quot;as large as they need to be&quot; dream-logic, with mile-long hospital corridors and endlessly sprawling wilderness?<br /> <br /> 3. Outside of Lair traits, how much control does the Beast have over how the Chambers appear? If a Chamber is made from an average two-story suburban house, can it be nightmare-stretched with extra rooms and whatnot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T20:25:56-08:00","id":815205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery#post815175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Rules are given for antagonists collapsing a Lair's Chambers, but how would they know such a thing was possible in the first place (excepting Heroes, who would probably intuit it the same way they do Anathemas)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, honestly, most of the time? They won't, they'll have no idea and no method of accessing that information. It's probably outside the domain of Occult, even assisted by a Library, though maybe not a Beast-specific Library. Mind-readers might have better luck, but that's not likely to be a surface thought and getting deep enough to start looking for supernatural weaknesses isn't a common skill. The inevitable appropriate Hunter organization might get fiat tipoffs and might not.<br /> <br /> Who's the exception? Mages, of course. They possess the means in spades, and are also the most likely to be interested in tramping around your Lair in the first place. For most other people, the goal they'll be pursuing related to your Lair is GETTING OUT.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery#post815175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How large are Chambers? ... &quot;as large as they need to be&quot; dream-logic, with mile-long hospital corridors and endlessly sprawling wilderness?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one sounds right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery#post815175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of Lair traits, how much control does the Beast have over how the Chambers appear? If a Chamber is made from an average two-story suburban house, can it be nightmare-stretched with extra rooms and whatnot?</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as it's one Chamber, that seems reasonable. I'm tempted to say something about remembering to differentiate between cosmetics and abusing the rule of cool for evil, but I feel like it's not going to come up a lot given how Lair traits work and how you pretty much have enough space for whatever you plan to do anyway. An average two-story suburban home is pretty easy to convert into a labyrinth if you go around bricking up the doors, for instance, and playing house of <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">leaves </span>is about the only thing I could come up with that isn't immediately just doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T20:45:50-08:00","id":815216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery#post815175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Outside of Lair traits, how much control does the Beast have over how the Chambers appear? If a Chamber is made from an average two-story suburban house, can it be nightmare-stretched with extra rooms and whatnot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Question on this one. Do you mean at the time of the Chamber's construction, or are you talking like adding traits to a Chamber as the Beast grows*?<br /> <br /> <br /> *Like the Beast grows and incorporates no escape into its Chamber traits and so a previously built labyrinth suddenly has it where even if you find the exit you still can't open the bloody thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:04:59-08:00","id":815500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815216#post815216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on this one. Do you mean at the time of the Chamber's construction, or are you talking like adding traits to a Chamber as the Beast grows*?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean excluding Lair Traits altogether. The two-story house is still spiritually a two-story house, maybe even recognizably the same two-story house that's on Elm Street, even though it now has 27 rooms, an eternally stocked kitchen, and a basement larger than an aircraft hanger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T10:33:42-08:00","id":815565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815500#post815500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean excluding Lair Traits altogether. The two-story house is still spiritually a two-story house, maybe even recognizably the same two-story house that's on Elm Street, even though it now has 27 rooms, an eternally stocked kitchen, and a basement larger than an aircraft hanger.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically could a Beast make the chamber a beach even though the point it was made at was inside a factory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:34:27-08:00","id":815662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815565#post815565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So basically could a Beast make the chamber a beach even though the point it was made at was inside a factory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. For example, a Beast creates a chamber during blizzard, but has no blizzard trait. Does the blizzard in the chamber last ''forever''? I don't think so. The Chamber is the reflection of the real world with Lair traits as bonuses.<br /> <br /> If the real world changes, the chamber changes too. For example, a chamber was created inside a factory. Lair traits are poor light and steam. In one year, the factory will be destroyed and a new shopping mall will be build on the same place. What now? I assume, the chamber changes. Once you had a factory now a shopping mall. Originally the factory had poor light and there was a lot of steam. Now, the shopping mall has none. There are bright lights and no steam. BUT, when the beast opens the chamber - the poor light and steam comes back. As a GM I would also rule that sometimes the mall goes dark, for 1 or 2 seconds. Or, that some customers feel a strange hot air current, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:46:02-08:00","id":815786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815662#post815662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. For example, a Beast creates a chamber during blizzard, but has no blizzard trait. Does the blizzard in the chamber last ''forever''? I don't think so. The Chamber is the reflection of the real world with Lair traits as bonuses.<br /> <br /> If the real world changes, the chamber changes too. For example, a chamber was created inside a factory. Lair traits are poor light and steam. In one year, the factory will be destroyed and a new shopping mall will be build on the same place. What now? I assume, the chamber changes. Once you had a factory now a shopping mall. Originally the factory had poor light and there was a lot of steam. Now, the shopping mall has none. There are bright lights and no steam. BUT, when the beast opens the chamber - the poor light and steam comes back. As a GM I would also rule that sometimes the mall goes dark, for 1 or 2 seconds. Or, that some customers feel a strange hot air current, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it's a more or less platonic ideal of the real world, and since it runs on narrative logic, destroying the real place wouldn't be as dangerous as you make out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T00:52:53-08:00","id":815945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815662#post815662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the real world changes, the chamber changes too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get that idea?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, a chamber was created inside a factory. Lair traits are poor light and steam. In one year, the factory will be destroyed and a new shopping mall will be build on the same place. What now? </div> </div> </div>I think it'd remain a factory... Since chambers are formed from a single event, they don't seem like some dimension that reflects the current world. That's more the Shadow from Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-25-2016, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T02:37:36-08:00","id":815975,"title":"","content":"I think in the case of extreme changes to the material counterpart to a chamber, the chamber would remain as it always was, but lose its connection to it's original entrance. The abandoned factory still exists in the Astral, but the only way of getting to it is via another chamber, because there is no factory in the real world to go through.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you'd need to use an abandoned shop or the basement or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:45:17-08:00","id":816098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815975#post815975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the case of extreme changes to the material counterpart to a chamber, the chamber would remain as it always was, but lose its connection to it's original entrance. The abandoned factory still exists in the Astral, but the only way of getting to it is via another chamber, because there is no factory in the real world to go through.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you'd need to use an abandoned shop or the basement or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why Safe Place is a better investment than you'd think, as it would (and should) prevent sites that get used for forming Chambers from getting Plotted away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:55:10-08:00","id":817134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815945#post815945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get that idea?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it'd remain a factory... Since chambers are formed from a single event, they don't seem like some dimension that reflects the current world. That's more the Shadow from Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, your opinion is that at the time the Beast creates a Chamber it actually makes a snapshot of the place. Well, in that case it would have to make a snapshot of the place at it is. If the factory was also a for example a maze, exactly as the Lair trait (that is actually realistic) the GM has a problem. Because the Beast has only 2 Lair traits - poor light and steam. With this snapshot logic the Beast also gets a &quot;free&quot; Maze Lair Trait, that actually lasts forever. I think, that the Beast does not make a ever-lasting snapshot of the place when creating a Chamber. As a GM I would allow the Beast the &quot;free&quot; Maze trait, but only so long as the actual maze in the real world last. The Beast other Lair Traits (poor light and steam) last forever (they were bought). When the factory (or just the maze inside) is destroyed in the real world, the Chamber changes adequatelly.<br /> Also, when you start using my logic, the Beast does not get a &quot;free&quot; Lair Trait when the Chamber is created during Blizzard, Extreme Cold, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:57:30-08:00","id":817137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815975#post815975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the case of extreme changes to the material counterpart to a chamber, the chamber would remain as it always was, but lose its connection to it's original entrance. The abandoned factory still exists in the Astral, but the only way of getting to it is via another chamber, because there is no factory in the real world to go through.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you'd need to use an abandoned shop or the basement or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would mean that a Hero does not have to enter the Lair to destroy/make useless a Chamber. He just have to destroy the place where the Chamber has its entrance. That is from my point of view unacceptable. Lairs are not that fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:58:03-08:00","id":817139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817134#post817134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, your opinion is that at the time the Beast creates a Chamber it actually makes a snapshot of the place. Well, in that case it would have to make a snapshot of the place at it is. If the factory was also a for example a maze, exactly as the Lair trait (that is actually realistic) the GM has a problem. Because the Beast has only 2 Lair traits - poor light and steam. With this snapshot logic the Beast also gets a &amp;quot;free&amp;quot; Maze Lair Trait, that actually lasts forever. I think, that the Beast does not make a ever-lasting snapshot of the place when creating a Chamber. As a GM I would allow the Beast the &amp;quot;free&amp;quot; Maze trait, but only so long as the actual maze in the real world last. The Beast other Lair Traits (poor light and steam) last forever (they were bought). When the factory (or just the maze inside) is destroyed in the real world, the Chamber changes adequatelly.<br /> Also, when you start using my logic, the Beast does not get a &amp;quot;free&amp;quot; Lair Trait when the Chamber is created during Blizzard, Extreme Cold, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not simply make it so that the Chamber only supplies the Lair Traits? Considering that Chambers seem to operate off dream logic, having a mazy factory that doesn't actually have the Maze trait seems sensible, relatively speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:04:55-08:00","id":817149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817139#post817139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not simply make it so that the Chamber only supplies the Lair Traits? Considering that Chambers seem to operate off dream logic, having a mazy factory that doesn't actually have the Maze trait seems sensible, relatively speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, this one Chamber has the additional Maze trait. Also, my point is, that this trait lasts only until the real maze in the real factory exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:17:27-08:00","id":817159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817134#post817134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, in that case it would have to make a snapshot of the place at it is. If the factory was also a for example a maze, exactly as the Lair trait (that is actually realistic) the GM has a problem. Because the Beast has only 2 Lair traits - poor light and steam. With this snapshot logic the Beast also gets a &quot;free&quot; Maze Lair Trait, that actually lasts forever. I think, that the Beast does not make a ever-lasting snapshot of the place when creating a Chamber. As a GM I would allow the Beast the &quot;free&quot; Maze trait, but only so long as the actual maze in the real world last. The Beast other Lair Traits (poor light and steam) last forever (they were bought). When the factory (or just the maze inside) is destroyed in the real world, the Chamber changes adequatelly.<br /> Also, when you start using my logic, the Beast does not get a &quot;free&quot; Lair Trait when the Chamber is created during Blizzard, Extreme Cold, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there is no sign at all in the text that it changes with the chambers real area. And considering it's formed from a Specific instance of fear.... it looks like it's made from Just that instance. It wouldn't get free lair traits. It's a dreamscape, it might not match the area perfectly. But it shouldn't change in any instance except for when you modify the traits of your lair chambers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T15:46:26-08:00","id":817220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817149#post817149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, this one Chamber has the additional Maze trait. Also, my point is, that this trait lasts only until the real maze in the real factory exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's odd I thought the chamber created in a street corner during a blizzard would have to give up steam or poor light if blizzard was a part of the terror that created the potential chamber.<br /> <br /> Edit: there is also the fact that the maze trait represents something of great difficulty where not having it means your maze would only stump a 3 year old with a broken crayon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 01-26-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T16:59:24-08:00","id":817251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=815975#post815975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the case of extreme changes to the material counterpart to a chamber, the chamber would remain as it always was, but lose its connection to it's original entrance. The abandoned factory still exists in the Astral, but the only way of getting to it is via another chamber, because there is no factory in the real world to go through.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you'd need to use an abandoned shop or the basement or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as extreme as you're phrasing implies there Elfive. Remember a chamber can be accessed from anywhere the Beast wants, it just becomes harder to more disconnected from the original location the entrance you're attempting to use is. So if you have a chamber in a factory then that factory is a door for the lair simple. If someone destroys the factory then you would need to recreate the events that allowed you to enter make the chamber at another factory for the easiest reentry, or you could use any factory without doing anything for a more extreme penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:09:17-08:00","id":817256,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, there's also using someone as a portal or going through another sort of otherworld barrier. What I meant is that they'd lose access to the easiest entry point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:21:32-08:00","id":817260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817134#post817134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, your opinion is that at the time the Beast creates a Chamber it actually makes a snapshot of the place. Well, in that case it would have to make a snapshot of the place at it is. If the factory was also a for example a maze, exactly as the Lair trait (that is actually realistic) the GM has a problem. Because the Beast has only 2 Lair traits - poor light and steam. With this snapshot logic the Beast also gets a &quot;free&quot; Maze Lair Trait, <b>that actually lasts forever</b>. I think, that the Beast does not make a ever-lasting snapshot of the place when creating a Chamber. As a GM I would allow the Beast the &quot;free&quot; Maze trait, but only so long as the actual maze in the real world last. The Beast other Lair Traits (poor light and steam) last forever (they were bought). When the factory (or just the maze inside) is destroyed in the real world, the Chamber changes adequatelly.<br /> Also, when you start using my logic, the Beast does not get a &quot;free&quot; Lair Trait when the Chamber is created during Blizzard, Extreme Cold, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: the Primordial, Pp. 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When she encounters a Chamber, whether the actual Chamber in the Primordial Dream or the physical analog in the waking world, the Beast instinctively knows it for what it is. She does not, however, automatically know what kind of supernatural being triggered the creation of the Chamber. If the Beast wishes to investigate the matter, she must remain in the area for a scene, studying the location, touching the walls or the ground, and letting her Horror \u201ctune in\u201d to the Chamber in the Primordial Dream. She can then glean some information about how the Chamber was formed. Chambers that are not part of a Lair still connect to one another via Primordial Pathways, and are part of the local hive. <b>Chambers formed this way last approximately five years, and then fade away into the Primordial Dream if not added to a Lair. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, a particularly intense event might resonate longer.</b> If multiple such events take place in a given location, the Chamber might grow larger and more diverse (encompassing more Traits).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:43:25-08:00","id":817915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817260#post817260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is the rule by unconnected Chambers, i.e. Chambers that are not part of a Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T22:22:14-08:00","id":818207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skydiver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=817915#post817915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that is the rule by unconnected Chambers, i.e. Chambers that are not part of a Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere does it say, &quot;Forever,&quot; it's set at 5 years, or an arbitrarily longer amount of time, set by the storyteller, i.e.: you. If you don't feel comfortable letting the character have access to the trait for longer than dramatically appropriate, then simply force those discovery rolls... or something. But why make the game less fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:42:01-08:00","id":818239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=818207#post818207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere does it say, &quot;Forever,&quot; it's set at 5 years, or an arbitrarily longer amount of time, set by the storyteller, i.e.: you. If you don't feel comfortable letting the character have access to the trait for longer than dramatically appropriate, then simply force those discovery rolls... or something. But why make the game less fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hex I think what Skydiver is saying is what argument does the rule for chambers created and connected to no Beast say about chambers that are actually hooked up to an active Beast's lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:57:03-08:00","id":818245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=818239#post818239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hex I think what Skydiver is saying is what argument does the rule for chambers created and connected to no Beast say about chambers that are actually hooked up to an active Beast's lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>And the answer to that is &quot;not a lot,&quot; because those Chambers are fading out, not changing.<br /> <br /> A Chamber is an Astral echo of a soul-shaking event and hooking it up to the Heart of a Beast just ties it into their Legend and the rest of their Lair. A Chamber can be formed at the scene of a burning building; the fact that there is no longer a building there has no bearing on the location's ties to the Primordial Dream, for all that it might make using the place for transit difficult under some readings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T21:43:15-08:00","id":818981,"title":"","content":"I don't see where your player is getting a &quot;free&quot; Lair Trait, as those are hard capped at the listed values in the Lair Table. It's not like accessing a Chamber automatically gives you control over its Traits. Also, the rules clearly state that unless the character has increased their Lair Rating, any new Traits gained through the addition of a Chamber get overwritten by the Beasts existing traits, as shown here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: the Primordial, Pp. 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once a Chamber is added to the Lair, it is set. Beasts can \u201ccollapse\u201d (remove) Chambers with effort, as described on p. 100. Intruders can force a collapse, but unless that happens Chambers stay in the Lair indefinitely. Once a Chamber becomes part of the Beast\u2019s Lair, it takes on the Traits of that Lair. <b>Any others fade.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 01-29-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T21:46:30-08:00","id":818982,"title":"","content":"As far as incorporating Chambers with extraneous Traits into one's own Lair goes, I think it's a reasonable guess that the manifestations of those Traits just diminish in activity or intensity unless you add them back in later or you have a broodmate with an appropriate Trait to piggyback off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-29-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T21:50:28-08:00","id":818984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=818982#post818982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Addressing the wrong person, Hex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, Satch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T03:42:05-08:00","id":819750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/815175-on-chambers-a-few-questions-about-load-bearing-scenery?p=818982#post818982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as incorporating Chambers with extraneous Traits into one's own Lair goes, I think it's a reasonable guess that the manifestations of those Traits just diminish in activity or intensity unless you add them back in later or you have a broodmate with an appropriate Trait to piggyback off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of my read on it, too. Setting elements like storms, burning buildings, riots . . . are all preserved by the Chamber (particularly if they contributed to the sanity break), but are &quot;nerfed&quot; if the Beast doesn't have the appropriate Lair trait.<br /> <br /> For example, taking a look at the &quot;blizzard&quot; Chamber idea, let's say the real world version was generated by a werewolf hunting a kid through a snowstorm. Lost in the snow, tripping and sliding through the snow, unable to see the path anymore . . . the kid's fear generates the chamber.<br /> <br /> Before a Beast claims the site, and applies any Lair traits, the original Chamber would be something like this:<ul><li>The Chamber itself is roughly circular, with a usable area that has a diameter of roughly 200 feet or so.</li> <li>The Chamber always feels cold, with icy winds blowing through it. It snows constantly, but not hard enough to obscure your view across the Chamber.</li> <li>While unpleasantly cold, and the average person wouldn't want to hang around without a coat/hat/gloves, a human can hang around indefinitely without suffering frostbite.</li> <li>There's roughly 3-6&quot; of snow on the ground, spread unevenly across the floor, forming into drifts, etc.</li> <li>Despite the constant snowstorm, the amount of snow on the ground never changes. The falling snow fills in footprints, covers up areas that people try to clear . . . but a careful observer will notice that while the drifts slowly shift, the overall amount of snow never increases or decreases.</li> <li>Individuals who try to leave the Chamber by walking out into the storm (rather than use a Burrow) will eventually hit a &quot;wall&quot; of fierce winds and blinding snow. Regardless of how good their sense of direction is, or how skilled they are at tracking, they will eventually stumble back out into the usable area of the Chamber. Mages (et al) who use their magic to track their progress will find that its not possible to walk more than five or ten feet past the usable area.</li> </ul>If a Beast wants the Chamber to be dangerously cold, or for the snow to come down hard enough to blind people, or for the drifts to be so deep they actively trip people, or . . . <i>then</i> they need to buy the relevant Lair traits. Otherwise, the Chamber is neutral, full of &quot;dream&quot; snow and &quot;phantom&quot; cold. Just an illusion, replicating the look and feel of the original site . . . but without the real world impact.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you could have a &quot;burning house&quot; Chamber full of &quot;dream&quot; fires, or a &quot;riot&quot; one where a &quot;phantom&quot; mob forms the walls (shoving people back out into the usable area of the room), or . . . A Chamber can be as narratively active as the player wants, and the original circumstances justify. Its one of the perks of hanging out with other supernaturals - the chance to find a Chamber where it perpetually rains blood, or one made out of candy, or that's the inside of someone's mouth . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: It would also be reasonable to argue that an unclaimed/wild Chamber would have all the Lair traits you'd expect it to have (dangerously cold, blinding snow, <i>et al</i>), and that the act of claiming it as part of your Lair &quot;nerfs&quot; them. Might give the Storyteller some extra setting options (sending Beasts/mages/etc into an unclaimed Chamber for some reason).<br /> <br /> Hmm . . . it might even be possible for a Beast to add a Chamber, and not &quot;nerf&quot; the wild Traits . . . but then they'd be just as dangerous to the Beast as to any uninvited guests . . . Have to think about that possibility some more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-30-2016, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}